{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginarchitecture"]}],"kind":"article","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Extend the dispatch cycle with lifecycle hooks — from invisible infrastructure to domain-specific features."}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ArchitectureGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/DesignPrinciples"],"anchor":"Explanation","generated":true,"title":"Explanation"}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}],"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article","title":"Plugin Architecture"},"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Swidux’s plugin system is a single protocol (","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SwiduxPlugin"},{"text":") with four lifecycle hooks and an ordered registry (","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginHost"},{"text":"). All store extensibility flows through this contract. The built-in ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin"},{"text":" use it, and so do domain-specific features like killswitch enforcement and paywall management.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"The-Dispatch-Lifecycle","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"The Dispatch Lifecycle"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Every call to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.send()"},{"text":" drives plugins through a four-phase lifecycle:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["plugins.willReduce(state:action:)      \/\/ 1. Pre-reduce (read-only state)","appReducer.reduce(state:action:...)    \/\/ 2. App reducer runs","pluginEffects = plugins.reduce(...)    \/\/ 3. Plugin reducers run","plugins.afterReduce(state:action:)     \/\/ 4. Post-reduce cleanup"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":null},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The generic ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store"},{"text":" implements this lifecycle internally. You don’t write ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"send()"},{"text":" by hand — ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Store.send()"},{"text":" handles packing, reducing, plugin hooks, unpacking, and effect dispatch.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A fifth method, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"flush()"},{"text":", runs once at shutdown to drain async buffers.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"All four hooks have default no-op implementations. Each plugin overrides only what it needs.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"Core-Middleware-vs-Domain-Plugins","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Core Middleware vs Domain Plugins"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The plugin system serves two structurally different roles. Recognizing which one a plugin fills determines where it lives, which hooks it uses, and how it couples to the host app.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"Core-Middleware","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Core Middleware"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin"},{"text":" are ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"action-agnostic infrastructure"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":". They never inspect the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Action"},{"text":" type, never dispatch actions, and never return effects. They couple only to the shape of state:","type":"text"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" needs keypaths to ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" properties.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" needs ","type":"text"},{"code":"State: Equatable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" so it can snapshot and compare.","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Because they don’t touch actions, they work with any app that uses Swidux — no wiring required beyond construction.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"Domain-Plugins","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Domain Plugins"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Killswitch, parental gate, and paywall plugins are ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"domain-specific modules"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" that ship as separate library targets (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxKillswitch"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxParentalGate"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxPaywall"},{"text":"). They own their own state slices and action enums, dispatch effects, and must be explicitly wired into the host app’s root types.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Each domain plugin stores three wiring pieces:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["private let stateKeyPath: WritableKeyPath<RootState, FeatureState>","private let toRootAction: @Sendable (FeatureAction) -> RootAction","private let extractAction: @Sendable (RootAction) -> FeatureAction?"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The host app provides these at init — the plugin never assumes a specific root type.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"Comparison","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Comparison"},{"type":"table","rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Core Middleware"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Domain Plugins"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Action knowledge","type":"text"}]}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"None"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Full — extracts and lifts actions"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Lifecycle hooks","type":"text"}]}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"willReduce"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"afterReduce"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reduce"},{"type":"text","text":" only"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Returns effects","type":"text"}]}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"No"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"State coupling","type":"text"}]}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Keypath to "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Equatable"},{"type":"text","text":" constraint"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Keypath to plugin’s own state slice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Wiring","type":"text"}]}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Construction only"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Keypath + action lifter + action extractor"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Target","type":"text"}]}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Core "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Swidux"},{"type":"text","text":" library"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Separate library target"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Opt-in","type":"text"}]}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Instantiate and register"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Add state, action case, and register"}],"type":"paragraph"}]]],"header":"row"},{"anchor":"The-Decision-Rule","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"The Decision Rule"},{"type":"aside","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Does the middleware need to know your action type? If "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"no","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":", it’s core middleware — put it in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Swidux"},{"type":"text","text":" and use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"willReduce"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"afterReduce"},{"type":"text","text":". If "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"yes","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":", it’s a domain plugin — give it its own target and use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reduce"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"style":"important","name":"Important"},{"anchor":"Hook-Selection-Guide","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Hook Selection Guide"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"willReduce(state:action:)"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — Capture state ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"before"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" the reducer mutates it. State is read-only. Use for snapshots (undo) or pre-mutation analytics.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reduce(state:action:) -> Effect?"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — Handle domain-specific actions ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"after"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" the app reducer. Mutate the plugin’s state slice and return effects. This is the only hook that can dispatch actions or do async work.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"afterReduce(state:action:)","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" — Observe state "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"after","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" all reducing is done. Use for persistence draining, logging, or metrics. Cannot return effects."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"flush() async"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" — Shutdown hook. Flush pending async buffers (persistence writes, analytics batches). Called once when the app exits."}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"anchor":"Registration-Order","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Registration Order"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginHost"},{"text":" executes plugins in registration order. Recommended ordering:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["let plugins = PluginHost<AppState, AppAction>()","plugins.register(undoPlugin)         \/\/ 1. Must snapshot before any mutation","plugins.register(persistencePlugin)  \/\/ 2. Drains changelogs after reducer","plugins.register(killswitchPlugin)   \/\/ 3. Domain plugins in any order","plugins.register(paywallPlugin)"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Undo must come first — it snapshots state in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"willReduce"},{"text":", before the app reducer or any plugin modifies it. Persistence typically comes next so its ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"afterReduce"},{"text":" drain sees the final state. Domain plugins use only ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reduce"},{"text":", so their relative order rarely matters.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"Service-Result-Actions-and-Transition-Observation","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Service-Result Actions and Transition Observation"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"service-result action"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" — ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PaywallPlugin"},{"text":"’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"customerInfoUpdated"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"KillswitchPlugin"},{"text":"’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"verdictReceived"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FeatureFlagsPlugin"},{"text":"’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"refreshSucceeded"},{"text":" — fires on ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"every"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" fetch, refresh, or stream tick, not","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"only when the value changed, and unconditionally writes its payload to the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"state slice. The payload is frequently identical to what is already there","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(a re-delivered entitlement, an unchanged remote config).","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Do ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"not"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" map analytics or side effects to the raw service-result action:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it fires duplicates by design. Observe the ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"state slice"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — or a value","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"derived from it — instead.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"State observation is already deduplicated by the framework. ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Store.send"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"packs the observer into a value-type snapshot, lets reducers mutate the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"snapshot, then writes back via ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"State.apply"},{"text":". For a leaf slice that write","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is a plain assignment whose ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Observable"},{"text":" setter equality-gates ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Equatable"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"values, so a slice whose value did not change emits no notification — and a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"value-diffing consumer such as ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AnalyticsIdentity.userProperties"},{"text":" (which","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AnalyticsPlugin"},{"text":" re-evaluates and diffs every non-analytics dispatch) sees exactly the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"real transitions. This dedup is a property of the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Store"},{"text":", not of any","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"per-plugin guard, so a no-op service-result cycle is silent to state","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"observers without any extra reducer logic.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"Next-Steps","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Next Steps"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingADomainPlugin","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" — Step-by-step guide to creating a domain plugin"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" — Configure the built-in persistence middleware"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoRedo","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" — Add undo\/redo with the built-in undo middleware"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"]]},"references":{"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/UndoRedo":{"type":"topic","title":"Undo \/ Redo","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Add stack-based undo\/redo to your app with "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/undoredo","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoRedo","kind":"article","role":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/UndoPlugin":{"type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"UndoPlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"UndoPlugin","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"UndoPlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Snapshot-based undo\/redo plugin."}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/undoplugin","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide":{"type":"topic","title":"Persistence Middleware","abstract":[{"type":"text","te